<div class="reading-column-wide">
  <header class="mb-4">
    <h1>
      <%= link_to book_path(book) do %>
        <%= book.title %>
      <% end %>
    </h1>
    <p class="webhooks-subtitle">
      Twist rebuilds this book when GitHub tells it the repository has changed.
      Point a webhook at the URL below to turn that on.
    </p>
  </header>

  <h2>Webhook URL</h2>

  <pre class="webhook-url"><code><%= receive_url %></code></pre>

  <h2>Setting it up on GitHub</h2>

  <ol class="webhook-steps">
    <li>
      Open the book's repository on GitHub, then go to
      <strong>Settings &rarr; Webhooks &rarr; Add webhook</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Paste the URL above into <strong>Payload URL</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Set <strong>Content type</strong> to
      <code>application/x-www-form-urlencoded</code>. Twist reads the push
      payload from the form's <code>payload</code> field, so
      <code>application/json</code> will not work.
    </li>
    <li>
      Leave <strong>Secret</strong> empty &mdash; Twist does not verify webhook
      signatures yet, so anyone who knows this URL can ask for a rebuild.
      Nothing but a rebuild can be triggered through it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Under <strong>Which events</strong>, choose
      <strong>Just the push event</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Keep <strong>Active</strong> ticked and save.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    Every push then arrives here, is recorded in the table below, and queues a
    background job that clones the repository at that commit and reprocesses the
    book's chapters. Pushing to a branch Twist has not seen before creates that
    branch.
  </p>

  <h2>Recently received</h2>

  <% if webhooks.any? %>
    <div class="webhook-table-scroll">
      <table class="webhook-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Received</th>
            <th>Event</th>
            <th>Branch</th>
            <th>Delivery</th>
            <th>Job</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% webhooks.each do |webhook| %>
            <tr>
              <td>
                <time datetime="<%= webhook.received_at.utc.iso8601 %>" title="<%= webhook.received_at.utc.strftime("%e %B %Y, %H:%M UTC") %>">
                  <%= distance_of_time_in_words Time.now.utc, webhook.received_at.utc, highest_measure_only: true %> ago
                </time>
              </td>
              <td><%= webhook.event || "push" %></td>
              <td>
                <span title="<%= webhook.ref %>"><%= webhook_branch(webhook) %></span>
              </td>
              <td>
                <% if webhook.delivery_id %>
                  <code class="webhook-delivery" title="<%= webhook.delivery_id %>"><%= webhook.delivery_id[0, 8] %></code>
                <% else %>
                  <span class="webhook-muted">&mdash;</span>
                <% end %>
              </td>
              <td>
                <span class="<%= webhook_status_class(webhook) %>"><%= webhook_status_label(webhook) %></span>

                <% if webhook_job_duration(webhook) %>
                  <span class="webhook-muted">in <%= webhook_job_duration(webhook) %></span>
                <% end %>

                <% if webhook.job_id %>
                  <div class="webhook-muted">job <code><%= webhook.job_id %></code></div>
                <% end %>

                <% if webhook.job_error %>
                  <div class="webhook-error"><%= webhook.job_error %></div>
                <% end %>
              </td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <p>
      <em class="text-gray-600">
        No webhooks have been received for this book yet. Push to the repository,
        or use <strong>Redeliver</strong> on an existing delivery in GitHub, and
        it will show up here.
      </em>
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>
